-- title:
--   Tate curve modulo order-d toric subgroup has j-invariant j(qᵈ)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $L$ a field equipped with an algebra structure over the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$, $N$ a nonzero natural number and $\zeta \in K$ a primitive $N$-th root of unity. Let $P$ be a point of the affine model of $((\mathrm{tateLaurent}\,K).\mathrm{baseChange}\,L)$, the base change to $L$ of the Tate Weierstrass curve $\langle 1,0,0,\mathrm{tateA4},\mathrm{tateA6}\rangle$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ obtained from the integral model by the coefficient map $\mathrm{laurentOfInt}\,K$. Assume: for every natural $n$, $n \bullet P = 0$ if and only if $N \mid n$; and for every natural $n$ with $N \nmid n$ the multiple $n \bullet P$ is the affine point whose coordinates are the images under the structure map $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K \to L$ of the two components of the toric point $\mathrm{toricPoint}\,K\,1\,(\zeta^n)$ (the explicit pair of Laurent series in $q$ whose coefficients are the divisor sums attached to the parameter $c = \zeta^n$), together with the corresponding nonsingularity witness. Let $d$ be a nonzero natural number dividing $N$, and let $H'$ be an additive subgroup of the points of the base-changed curve which is cyclic, has cardinality $d$, and is contained in the subgroup generated by $P$. Then $\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,H'\,d$ for the base-changed curve — that is, $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the curve $\mathrm{cyclicQuotientCurve}\,H'\,d$ produced by the iterated Vélu construction — equals the image in $L$ of $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,d = \mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,d\,(\mathrm{jqModC}\,K)$, i.e. of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral }j\text{-numerator series})$ with $q$ replaced by $q^{d}$.
--
--   This is the Tate-curve computation $j(E_q/\mu_d) = j(q^d)$, reflecting the isogeny $\mathbb{G}_m/q^{\mathbb{Z}} \to \mathbb{G}_m/q^{d\mathbb{Z}}$, $u \mapsto u^d$, in the formal setting of Weierstrass models over $K((q))$ and their iterated Vélu quotients. It supplies the $q$-expansion input for identifying the value of $j(q^d)$ at a moduli point of a pair $(E,H)$, and is used by the results on $j$-invariants of cyclic quotients of base-changed Tate curves and by the classification of level structures on them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_cyclicQuotientJ_tateLaurent_baseChange_eq_jqNModC_of_le_zmultiples.lean

